From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Report the PS5's 120 Hz output rate.

The PS5 user driver reported its one mode at 60 Hz. A title can ask
the video output for 119.88 Hz on a 120 Hz TV, and every Vulkan game
then presents at that rate, but EnumDisplaySettings, DXGI's mode list
and D3D9's adapter modes still said 60. DXVK limits a fullscreen D3D9
game with VSync to the rate its mode reports, so such a game never
went past 60 frames per second.

The driver now reports 120 Hz when the title sets
PS5_VIDEOOUT_REFRESH=120, and 60 Hz otherwise. win32u then lists every
mode at both 60 and 120 Hz, the current one at 120. It is the rate the
title asked for, not the one the TV took: a display query cannot ask
Vulkan. If the TV refuses 120 Hz, the output stays at 60 and DXVK's
limit of 120 does nothing. ChangeDisplaySettings still accepts any rate
a game sets.
---
 dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
index da9cc05..78f0839 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -217,6 +217,19 @@ static void present_screen_for_change(void)
 /***********************************************************************
  *           display
  */
+/* The rate the title asks the video output for, 120 or 60 (a game's
+ * [display] refresh). DXVK limits a game to the rate its mode reports, so
+ * a game on a 120 Hz output must see 120. It is the rate asked for, not
+ * the one the TV took, which only Vulkan knows, and a display query must
+ * not wait on Vulkan (loaderdrv_VulkanInit). If the TV refuses 120, the
+ * output stays at 60 and a limit of 120 does nothing. */
+static UINT display_frequency(void)
+{
+    const char *refresh = getenv( "PS5_VIDEOOUT_REFRESH" );
+
+    return refresh && !strcmp( refresh, "120" ) ? 120 : 60;
+}
+
 static UINT ps5_UpdateDisplayDevices( const struct gdi_device_manager *manager, void *param )
 {
     struct pci_id pci_id = {0};
@@ -229,7 +242,7 @@ static UINT ps5_UpdateDisplayDevices( const struct gdi_device_manager *manager,
     mode.dmBitsPerPel = 32;
     mode.dmPelsWidth = screen_width;
     mode.dmPelsHeight = screen_height;
-    mode.dmDisplayFrequency = 60;
+    mode.dmDisplayFrequency = display_frequency();
 
     SetRect( &monitor.rc_monitor, 0, 0, screen_width, screen_height );
     monitor.rc_work = monitor.rc_monitor;
